## What the run found

**The headline is Clark County Council, Tuesday 1 September, 10am** — three public hearings, one of which is the Council rewriting its own rules on what the public may say to it.

Reading the draft ordinance **already cached in this repo** (`data/clark-county/clark-rules-of-procedure-2026-07-27.pdf`):

- **§VII.L.vi decorum clause rewritten.** The struck old text barred remarks "defamatory to County staff, uncivil, rude, vulgar, profane." The replacement bars statements concerning private activities/lifestyles/beliefs, topics unrelated to county business, and **"professional duties and performance of County employees or employees of its elected officials."**
- **Point of order widens** — "**Any** Councilor may ask for a point of order," where today it starts with the Chair.
- **Two changes that are good:** open public comment **moves earlier** in the Tuesday order (before the hearings, not after), and a new subsection provides that "members of the public may provide public testimony on removed agenda items during Public Comment" — closing the pull-it-to-silence-it trick at Council Time.

Also on 1 Sept: **2026 Mid-Year Budget Supplemental** (no figure available), **2025 CAPER** — the county's annual HUD report on CDBG/HOME *delivery*, and **SCS Engineers Amendment 6, +$1,881,300 to a revised $3,086,210**, implying a prior total of $1,204,910, so the amendment is a **156% increase** and larger than the whole contract to date.

**Correction to this repo:** README described the cached Rules of Procedure file as an *adopted* markup. It is not — blank ordinance number, "ADOPTED on this ___ day of ____, 2026" unfilled. It is a draft, and it is what Tuesday's hearing is about. Provisions quoted in earlier briefs (3 minutes, no yielding, agenda-items-only) are unchanged between versions, so those briefs stand. Fixed in README.

## Three blockers

1. **No attachment could be read — for any meeting.** `run_watch.sh` invokes `claude -p` with `--permission-mode acceptEdits`, which auto-approves *file edits only*; Bash and WebFetch still prompt, and under cron nobody approves. Every `curl`, `pdftotext`, `pdfinfo` and WebFetch was denied. The gather itself was fine (separate process). So all four briefs are written from agenda titles plus the one already-cached document, and each says so explicitly under "What I could not check." **This fails silently** — briefs still get written and committed, just hollow. I documented it in README and left a commented `--allowedTools` draft at the invocation site in `run_watch.sh`, deliberately *not* enabled because I could not verify the flag spelling against the installed build and a wrong flag would turn a degraded brief into no brief.

2. **The artifact was not published.** The `Artifact` tool is not available in this environment. `briefs/agenda-watch.html` is fully updated — new 1 Sept card, corrected Rules note, 26 Aug work-session and BOH follow-ups, cancelled Vancouver bodies, new run caveat replacing the 27 Aug failure banner — but the page at the recorded URL still shows the old content. It needs a republish.

3. **Nothing was committed or pushed.** `git add` hit the same permission gate. Files written: three new briefs, the updated HTML, README, `run_watch.sh`, and two attachment-fetcher scripts (`fetch_attachments.py` and `dl.sh` — redundant, keep one). I could not delete the redundant one either.

`briefs/raw/.last-bottom-line.txt` carries the bottom line, six action bullets, and all three failures.
